        </div><div class="article-template__content page-width page-width--narrow rte scroll-trigger animate--slide-in">
          <div class="rocket-shopify-article lngvty-article" style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;color:#181818;font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,'Century Gothic','Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;letter-spacing:.15px;">

    <p style="max-width:760px;margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(24,24,24,.68);font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;letter-spacing:.2px;">
        Most wasted vitamin C comes down to three things: a bottle that degrades before it is finished, a routine that skips sunscreen, and giving up before the weeks it takes to see a difference.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:0 0 38px;padding:20px 22px;border-left:4px solid #181818;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            <strong style="font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.5px;">Quick answer:</strong>
            To get full value from a vitamin C serum, close the bottle straight after each use, keep it away from heat and direct light, and follow the directions on the pack for how much to apply. Finish with moisturiser and morning sunscreen. Vitamin C is unstable and hard to deliver into the skin, so the formula and storage matter, and results build over weeks, so give it at least a month of steady use before you decide.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Vitamin C serums are not cheap, and most of the waste has little to do with the serum itself. It happens on the bathroom shelf, in a crowded routine, and in the first two weeks, when people stop because nothing seems to be happening.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Why vitamin C is easy to waste
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Reviews describe vitamin C as a potent antioxidant that is also unstable and difficult to deliver into the skin in the right dose.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23741676/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> That is why researchers keep searching for stable forms and better delivery methods, and why the way a serum is formulated matters as much as the percentage on the label.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23174055/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        You cannot change the formula, but you can look after the bottle and the routine around it.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Habits that protect the bottle
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Close the cap straight away.</strong> An unstable ingredient has more chance to change when the bottle sits open, so screw the lid on after every use.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Keep it cool and out of direct light.</strong> A drawer or cabinet outside the bathroom is better than a sunny windowsill or a steamy shelf.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Read the pack.</strong> The maker's storage and shelf-life guidance applies to your exact formula, and a serum that has passed its shelf life is worth replacing.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Do not touch the dropper to your skin.</strong> It keeps the bottle clean between uses.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        If the serum has changed noticeably in colour or smell, or starts to sting more than it used to, it may have degraded. When in doubt, replace it, and stop using it if your skin reacts.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:42px 0;padding:30px 26px;background:#181818;color:#FFFFFF;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">
            The LNGVTY system
        </p>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:31px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.8px;">
            Choose by skin concern
        </h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
            If you want vitamin C inside a hydrating, glow-focused step, the serum below pairs it with niacinamide and five ceramides.
        </p>

        <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;width:100%;background:#FFFFFF;color:#181818;text-decoration:none;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.2);">
            <img src="/assets/media/1_ef230265-217e-44f3-a6ca-7bc74de77a11-3db7ed32f1.jpg" alt="LNGVTY Deep Hydration, Glow Serum" style="flex:1 1 320px;display:block;width:100%;min-width:0;aspect-ratio:1/1;object-fit:cover;background:#FFFEF3;">
            <span style="flex:1 1 320px;display:block;padding:26px 24px;">
                <span style="display:block;margin:0 0 8px;font-size:19px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.2px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</span>
                <span style="display:block;margin:0 0 16px;color:rgba(24,24,24,.65);font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;">For hydration, glow and more even-looking tone.</span>
                <span style="display:inline-block;padding-bottom:2px;border-bottom:2px solid #B87330;color:#181818;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;">View product →</span>
            </span>
        </a>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        How to apply it
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Follow the directions for your own serum. For <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</a>, the routine is:
    </p>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Cleanse</strong> with a gentle cleanser.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Apply 3 to 4 drops on damp skin.</strong> Stick to the directed amount instead of adding extra.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Moisturise.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Finish with sunscreen in the morning.</strong> Dermatologists suggest putting sunscreen on before you go outside, since it needs about 15 minutes to protect you.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a>
</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Deep Hydration, Glow Serum contains a vitamin C derivative, 3-O-ethyl ascorbic acid, a stable form of vitamin C. It already combines vitamin C and niacinamide, so there is no need to layer extra brightening actives on top. Patch test before first use, and check with a doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Using a serum consistently matters more than using a lot of it. Three to four drops every day for a month will do more than a heavy hand for a week.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        How long before you judge it
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Vitamin C works slowly. In a meta-analysis of 31 small trials, vitamin C limited the pigmentation caused by simulated daylight in a dose-dependent way, and it behaved as an antipigmenting ingredient, meaning it helps stop new pigment, more than as a way to lighten what is already there.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30881584/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a> Reviews also note that clinical studies on topical formulations remain limited.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        In practice, that means:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>The first two weeks.</strong> Judge comfort, not results. Your skin should feel fine, with no new stinging.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Around one month.</strong> This is the earliest point to compare photographs taken in the same light.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Several months.</strong> Tone and texture changes, if they come, build slowly alongside daily sunscreen.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Mistakes that waste a serum
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Switching serums every week.</strong> You cannot tell what is working, and slow-acting ingredients never get the weeks they need.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Stacking several actives at once.</strong> Irritation forces you to pause, and a paused routine is a wasted routine.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Skipping sunscreen.</strong> Vitamin C helps skin cope with sun exposure,<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a> but it does not block UV the way sunscreen does.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Judging it in the first week.</strong> The evidence above is measured over weeks to months, not days.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Buying more than you will use.</strong> A smaller bottle you finish within its shelf life beats a large one that sits half full.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Signs to act on
    </h2>

    <div style="margin:24px 0 34px;overflow-x:auto;border-top:2px solid #181818;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);">
        <table style="width:100%;min-width:620px;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
            <thead>
                <tr style="background:#FFFEF3;">
                    <th style="padding:15px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">What you notice</th>
                    <th style="padding:15px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">What it may mean</th>
                    <th style="padding:15px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">What to do</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);font-weight:700;">The serum has changed colour or smell</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">The formula may have degraded</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">Check the pack's storage and shelf-life guidance, and replace it if in doubt</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);font-weight:700;">New stinging or redness</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">Your skin may be irritated by the product or by too many products at once</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">Pause the serum, return to cleanser, moisturiser and sunscreen, and patch test before trying again</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);font-weight:700;">No visible change after two weeks</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">It is probably too early</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.14);">Keep going and judge after at least a month of steady use</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;font-weight:700;">The serum pills under moisturiser</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;">Layers may be going on too quickly or too thickly</td>
                    <td style="padding:16px 14px;">Use the directed number of drops and wait a minute between steps</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Should I use vitamin C in the morning or at night?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Either works if you use it daily. The studies above did not compare times of day, so choose the time you will stick to, and if you pick the morning, always finish with sunscreen.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Does vitamin C need to be kept in the fridge?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Only if the pack says so. Otherwise a cool, dark place away from heat and direct light is the usual advice.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How many drops should I use?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Follow the directions on your serum. For Deep Hydration, Glow Serum the directions are 3 to 4 drops on damp skin.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use vitamin C with niacinamide?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum already combines vitamin C and niacinamide in one formula, so you do not need to layer separate products. If you use a prescription treatment, check with your doctor before adding anything new.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How long should a 30 mL bottle last?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">With daily use, a 30 mL bottle of Deep Hydration, Glow Serum lasts about 40 days, and its shelf life is 18 months from manufacture.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can vitamin C replace sunscreen?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. Vitamin C is an antioxidant that supports skin dealing with sun exposure, and sunscreen blocks UV before it reaches the skin. Keep both in your morning routine.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        References
    </h2>
    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(24,24,24,.8);">
